# The QA verify's -Dit.test, one class per line. THE LIST IS NOT DERIVED: a class this file stops
# naming is written and never runs, silently, and there is no wildcard to fall back on — `*IT` would
# pull PackagedSurfaceIT back in, which does real git pushes through a CGI fixture and a
# pseudo-terminal and is why skipITs is true in the root pom to begin with.
#
# The five story classes come first and in this order, which is the order failsafe runs them in
# anyway (it orders by FQCN within a @TestProfile group) and is load-bearing: they share one profile,
# TokenValidationBootstrapIT.PackagedWithMockIdp, so the group is one launched process and one
# embedded postgres, and the bootstrap IT owns the run's first bearer and the JWKS fetch after it.
# See AGENTS.md § Userflows.

TokenValidationBootstrapIT
ProjectCatalogueIT
EpicPlanningIT
AccessRefusalIT
CatalogueReviewIT

# The pin test, which is not a story and not in that profile group at all: plain JUnit, no
# @TestProfile, no Quarkus application, no bearer, so its position here decides nothing. It is the
# gate that makes this repository's image pin mean something — qits/project-agent, which a project's
# agent container starts (ProjectAgentImage.VERSION off the pinned qits-projects-daemon-protocol). It
# downloads the daemon at exactly the pinned version, runs it as a process against a stand-in host
# and round-trips the real protocol, so a daemon bump that breaks the wire fails THIS fold rather
# than the next live agent container. Drop the line and the pin is an untested number again. It needs
# the artifacts origin, which it derives by cutting qits.maven.repository.url at /artifacts/ — the
# archetype's verify exports and passes it; with no origin at all it skips, which is the one state a
# CI step is never in. Its refinement twin, RefinementDaemonPinIT, went with the refinement
# containers (qits-1316).

ProjectAgentDaemonPinIT
